  "verbalization": "Vitexin 2''-O-glucoside is implicated in the biological pathway leading to Neuropilin-2 through a series of molecular interactions. The evidence suggests that the compound targets CD70 antigen, which is subsequently recognized by Bastadin 12 or Aplysamine, both of which in turn target Neuropilin-2. This indicates a potential cascade where Vitexin 2''-O-glucoside may influence the expression or activity of CD70, thereby affecting the downstream signaling to Neuropilin-2. The presence of multiple pathways converging on Neuropilin-2 highlights the complexity of the interaction network, with Vitexin 2''-O-glucoside acting as a central node in this pathway. The integration of these findings suggests that the compound may modulate the expression or function of Neuropilin-2 through the CD70 pathway, potentially influencing cellular processes involving receptor signaling.",
